<title>FRANCE: Lagardere drops on Thomson fears.</title>
<headline>Lagardere drops on Thomson fears.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in missiles-to-books conglomerate Lagardere fell sharply on Monday, following market talk that its offer for the Thomson SA electronics group could fail due to legal and financial complications, traders said.</p>
<p>Negative sentiment was sparked by a report in business newspaper La Tribune Defosses which said, &quot;notes on the shortcomings in the legal and financial structure were circulating in the Council of State.&quot; The Council is France's highest administrative court.</p>
<p>Lagardere stock was down 5.40 francs, or 3.34 percent, at 156.10 francs at 1044 GMT.</p>
</text>
